    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 there's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`) with 2 tests, both passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation from city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a transient derived getter `getLocality()`, following the existing `getMembershipTier()` / `getMembershipNumber()` pattern for computed read-only fields:\n   ```java\n   private static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(\n       \"Sydney\", \"NSW\", \"Melbourne\", \"VIC\", \"Brisbane\", \"QLD\");\n\n   @Transient\n   public String getLocality() {\n       return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(this.city, \"UNKNOWN\");\n   }\n   ```\n   Returns the canonical region for a known city, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` otherwise (also handles absent city safely).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\nMapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps the field automatically by name (getter \u2192 DTO property), just as it does for the other derived fields, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 UNKNOWN) \u2014 both pass, and the full build is green.",
